.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt MSDOSFS 5
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm msdosfs
.Nd FAT file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
In
.Xr fstab 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
/dev/gpt/efi	/boot/efi	msdosfs	rw	2	2
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
file system reads and writes FAT12, FAT16 and FAT32 volumes, with long file
names: EFI system partitions, memory cards, USB sticks, and volumes shared with
other systems.
It is mounted with
.Xr mount_msdosfs 8 ,
or
.Xr mount 8
.Fl t Cm msdosfs .
.Pp
FAT keeps no owners, permissions or links.
Every file belongs to the mount's owner and group, with the mount's permissions
.Pq Xr mount_msdosfs 8 Fl u , Fl g , Fl m , Fl M ,
by default those of the directory mounted on; a file with FAT's read-only
attribute shows no write bits, and
.Xr chmod 2
sets or clears that attribute by the owner's write bit.
.Xr chown 2
to anything but the mount's owner and group,
.Xr link 2 ,
.Xr symlink 2
and
.Xr mknod 2
fail.
Every file shows one link.
.Pp
Names are case-insensitive and case-preserving: a name is found in any case,
under its long name or its short (8.3) alias, and is created as given.
Long names are UTF-8 on the system side and UTF-16 on the volume.
Short names are in a DOS code page, CP437 by default
.Pq Xr mount_msdosfs 8 Fl D .
A name FAT can't hold
.Pq a control character, or one of Qo \e * / : < > ? \e| Qc
is refused with
.Er EINVAL .
.Pp
FAT keeps local time, without a zone: times are converted with the kernel's
.Va kern.utc_offset ,
which
.Xr adjkerntz 8
sets.
FAT has no change time; the modification time stands in for it.
Access times are kept to the day.
.Pp
A file's inode number is where its directory entry is on the volume (a
directory's, where its first cluster is), as on
.Fx ;
renaming a file changes it.
.Pp
A FAT16 or FAT32 volume is marked unclean while it is mounted read-write, and
clean again when unmounted.
One not marked clean when mounted (the system stopped without unmounting it)
is mounted read-only, with a warning, unless the mount is forced
.Pq Xr mount 8 Fl f ;
check it with
.Xr fsck_msdosfs 8
first.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr adjkerntz 8 ,
.Xr fsck_msdosfs 8 ,
.Xr makefs 8 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr mount_msdosfs 8 ,
.Xr newfs_msdos 8
.Sh HISTORY
An
.Nm
file system first appeared in
.Bx 386 0.1
and
.Nx 0.8 .
OxideBSD's is its own, written for it.
.Sh BUGS
The FAT's other copies and the volume's data are written as the buffer cache
evicts them; a crash can leave lost clusters and FAT copies that differ, which
.Xr fsck_msdosfs 8
.Fl p
repairs.
